  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P(X<3\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.",
  "worked_solution": "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<3\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y>2) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(2,1),(2,2),(2,3),(3,3)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,1))+P((X,Y)=(2,2)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,3))+P((X,Y)=(3,3)) \\\\  & =f(2,1)+f(2,2)+f(2,3)+f(3,3) \\\\  & =0.1+0.15+0.3+0.15 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
